// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: sam0x90
// Date: 2021-08-06 | Modified: 2022-10-09
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1003, T1003.003, S0404
// Description: Conti recommendation to its affiliates to use esentutl to access NTDS dumped file. Trickbot also
//   uses this utilities to get MSEdge info via its module pwgrab.
// False positives:
//   - To be determined
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/vxunderground/status/1423336151860002816
//   - https://thedfirreport.com/2021/08/01/bazarcall-to-conti-ransomware-via-trickbot-and-cobalt-strike/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_esentutl_params.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "esentutl" and ProcessCommandLine contains " /p"
